## 8. Evaluate Probability of Improvement and Expected Improvement

As an additional final check, the selected candidates were reassessed using Probability of Improvement (PI), Expected Improvement (EI) and a conservative prediction score.

PI estimates the probability that a candidate's output will exceed the current best under the GP predictive distribution.

EI considers both the probability and expected magnitude of potential improvement.

The conservative score was calculated by subtracting the GP's predictive standard deviation from its predicted mean.

These measures offered different perspectives on candidate quality.

A high EI could result from substantial uncertainty rather than a strong predicted mean, while a high PI could favour a candidate offering only a very small improvement.

